WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.427 --> 00:00:03.467
(dramatic crescendo)

00:00:03.467 --> 00:00:04.300
- Hello, Believe Nation!

00:00:04.300 --> 00:00:07.466
Today we're going to talk about
how you can handle bullying.

00:00:07.466 --> 00:00:08.903
Rule number one is my personal favorite,

00:00:08.903 --> 00:00:11.319
and I'd love to know which
one you guys like the best.

00:00:11.319 --> 00:00:12.941
As always guys, as you're
watching the clips,

00:00:12.941 --> 00:00:15.157
and you hear somebody say something that

00:00:15.157 --> 00:00:17.170
really resonates with you, please leave it

00:00:17.170 --> 00:00:18.889
in the comments below,
and put quotes around it,

00:00:18.889 --> 00:00:20.999
so other people can be inspired as well.

00:00:20.999 --> 00:00:23.198
Also when you write it
down, it's much more likely

00:00:23.198 --> 00:00:25.634
to stick with yourself, too.

00:00:25.634 --> 00:00:26.584
Enjoy.

00:00:26.584 --> 00:00:29.167
(upbeat music)

00:00:43.768 --> 00:00:44.640
- I've become an expert on this,

00:00:44.640 --> 00:00:46.836
because I was one of those
being bullied, (laughs),

00:00:46.836 --> 00:00:48.367
and most people wouldn't
think that about me,

00:00:48.367 --> 00:00:49.770
because I'm six seven, but I was actually

00:00:49.770 --> 00:00:51.589
always the smallest kid in my class.

00:00:51.589 --> 00:00:52.529
Part of what kept me going,

00:00:52.529 --> 00:00:54.052
was the vision in my mind that said,

00:00:54.052 --> 00:00:56.145
they may do this to me today, but someday

00:00:56.145 --> 00:00:58.056
my life will be more.

00:00:58.056 --> 00:00:59.990
I won't be the person
that people verbally,

00:00:59.990 --> 00:01:01.011
or physically abuse.

00:01:01.011 --> 00:01:02.919
And I remember being in high school,

00:01:02.919 --> 00:01:05.293
and envisioning some day
I was going to become

00:01:05.293 --> 00:01:07.880
this successful person, and I
was going to make a difference,

00:01:07.880 --> 00:01:11.437
and I'd become a financially successful.

00:01:11.437 --> 00:01:13.292
The fact that we had no
money, was one of the things

00:01:13.292 --> 00:01:14.931
that I was bullied about most.

00:01:14.931 --> 00:01:17.436
And I remember I signed
in a couple of these

00:01:17.436 --> 00:01:19.736
bullies' annuals at the end of the year.

00:01:19.736 --> 00:01:20.893
I got a hold of their annuals, and I wrote

00:01:20.893 --> 00:01:21.726
these horrible things.

00:01:21.726 --> 00:01:23.104
I became the bully, right?

00:01:23.104 --> 00:01:24.493
They didn't know, and I
wrote these horrible things.

00:01:24.493 --> 00:01:26.419
Saying, some day you'll be a truck driver,

00:01:26.419 --> 00:01:27.603
and I'll be rich and famous.

00:01:27.603 --> 00:01:29.297
And you'll be there, wishing you were me,

00:01:29.297 --> 00:01:30.280
and treated me better.

00:01:30.280 --> 00:01:33.289
So I went to my 10 year
high school reunion.

00:01:33.289 --> 00:01:34.596
I talked to my mom,
and my mom has not been

00:01:34.596 --> 00:01:36.557
much of a coach in my life, quite frankly,

00:01:36.557 --> 00:01:38.582
but that day she was really interesting.

00:01:38.582 --> 00:01:39.951
She said, what's going on?

00:01:39.951 --> 00:01:41.647
I said, oh I'm going on my
10 year high school reunion,

00:01:41.647 --> 00:01:44.041
and I just want to say hello,
and I'm driving my way up.

00:01:44.041 --> 00:01:46.128
And she goes, honey I can
hear something in your voice.

00:01:46.128 --> 00:01:46.961
What is it?

00:01:46.961 --> 00:01:47.939
I said, nothing.

00:01:47.939 --> 00:01:49.475
And what it was, when
I was going up there,

00:01:49.475 --> 00:01:51.291
I remembered what it was
like 10 years before,

00:01:51.291 --> 00:01:56.182
when I felt so alone, when
I felt totally an outsider.

00:01:56.182 --> 00:01:58.486
When I felt, I feared for
what was going to happen to me

00:01:58.486 --> 00:02:01.543
physically, or at least getting harassed.

00:02:01.543 --> 00:02:05.601
And I felt just so
different, outside and alone.

00:02:05.601 --> 00:02:07.493
And she said, honey, she said
I didn't tell her any of that.

00:02:07.493 --> 00:02:09.371
And she said, honey, you
were always the outsider,

00:02:09.371 --> 00:02:11.363
you were always the loner.

00:02:11.363 --> 00:02:13.224
And she goes, look what
being different got you.

00:02:13.224 --> 00:02:14.945
She goes, now how many people
were in you high school?

00:02:14.945 --> 00:02:16.541
And I said, I don't know, 2,000.

00:02:16.541 --> 00:02:18.872
She goes, 5,000 people
show up to hear you speak.

00:02:18.872 --> 00:02:19.717
(laughs)

00:02:19.717 --> 00:02:21.093
she said, for one weekend.

00:02:21.093 --> 00:02:22.452
She said, look what that's done.

00:02:22.452 --> 00:02:23.945
And that's what I try
to tell the young people

00:02:23.945 --> 00:02:24.943
who are going through it.

00:02:24.943 --> 00:02:26.561
Once again, it's not where you start out,

00:02:26.561 --> 00:02:28.653
it's where you end up.

00:02:28.653 --> 00:02:31.574
Some of the toughest experiences
life will give you drive,

00:02:31.574 --> 00:02:33.252
if you don't let it destroy you.

00:02:33.252 --> 00:02:35.303
If you realize that this
person who is a bully,

00:02:35.303 --> 00:02:39.053
is often a bully because
they're massively insecure.

00:02:39.053 --> 00:02:40.520
And just go, this is temporary.

00:02:40.520 --> 00:02:41.826
And get yourself with
a peer group of people

00:02:41.826 --> 00:02:43.822
who respect you, you
love you, appreciate you.

00:02:43.822 --> 00:02:45.537
Who you appreciate and love, and spend

00:02:45.537 --> 00:02:47.127
more of your time there.

00:02:47.127 --> 00:02:48.876
You'll find yourself, if you're filled up

00:02:48.876 --> 00:02:50.528
by the rest of your life, you can handle

00:02:50.528 --> 00:02:51.923
the challenges there.

00:02:51.923 --> 00:02:53.520
If it gets physical, then you got to go

00:02:53.520 --> 00:02:55.968
to some authority that can
help stop that situation,

00:02:55.968 --> 00:02:57.682
if you can't protect yourself.

00:02:57.682 --> 00:03:00.483
- Growing up Asian American,
and trying to play basketball,

00:03:00.483 --> 00:03:02.171
was really tough at times.

00:03:02.171 --> 00:03:03.683
Sometimes people would make fun of me,

00:03:03.683 --> 00:03:05.887
and they would just say,
oh, you're Yao Ming?

00:03:05.887 --> 00:03:07.736
You know, that's not that bad.

00:03:07.736 --> 00:03:09.109
Sometimes it would get a little worse.

00:03:09.109 --> 00:03:10.869
They would say, oh,
you're a Chinese import.

00:03:10.869 --> 00:03:12.542
Go back to China.

00:03:12.542 --> 00:03:15.210
Or, can you see the
scoreboard with your eyes?

00:03:15.210 --> 00:03:16.714
And sometimes it got really ridiculous.

00:03:16.714 --> 00:03:19.078
People would call me just chink, or gook,

00:03:19.078 --> 00:03:21.965
or just racist terms like that.

00:03:21.965 --> 00:03:23.826
And I remember one time
I got really upset.

00:03:23.826 --> 00:03:27.309
Kind of lost control, and
responded really negatively.

00:03:27.309 --> 00:03:30.102
And my coach kind of
told me after the game,

00:03:30.102 --> 00:03:33.377
he said, Jeremy, when
people say that to you,

00:03:33.377 --> 00:03:36.497
they're just trying to get in your head.

00:03:36.497 --> 00:03:38.151
And honestly, the best thing to do is

00:03:38.151 --> 00:03:40.217
take that negative energy, and turn it

00:03:40.217 --> 00:03:41.332
into positive energy.

00:03:41.332 --> 00:03:43.933
Fuel yourself, motivate
yourself with that.

00:03:43.933 --> 00:03:45.683
Don't react in anger.

00:03:46.541 --> 00:03:49.208
And so my lesson that I learned,

00:03:50.424 --> 00:03:52.853
and if there's anything I
can pass on to you guys is,

00:03:52.853 --> 00:03:55.415
a lot of times, bullies
like to bully other people

00:03:55.415 --> 00:03:57.859
because of certain insecurities
they have themselves.

00:03:57.859 --> 00:04:01.407
And so, don't let somebody
else tell you who you are,

00:04:01.407 --> 00:04:03.446
or what you can or can't do.

00:04:03.446 --> 00:04:05.360
Definitely look inside yourself.

00:04:05.360 --> 00:04:07.862
Have confidence in yourself,
believe in yourself,

00:04:07.862 --> 00:04:09.110
and understand what makes you such a

00:04:09.110 --> 00:04:10.696
unique and special person.

00:04:10.696 --> 00:04:14.728
Everybody has different and really cool

00:04:14.728 --> 00:04:16.653
characteristics, skills, talents.

00:04:16.653 --> 00:04:18.973
So never lose sight of that.

00:04:18.973 --> 00:04:22.190
Just always stay positive,
and hopefully one day,

00:04:22.190 --> 00:04:24.262
you'll take a look back
at these experiences,

00:04:24.262 --> 00:04:26.774
and realize hey, me getting bullied,

00:04:26.774 --> 00:04:28.585
or me having to go
through these experiences

00:04:28.585 --> 00:04:30.363
made me stronger.

00:04:30.363 --> 00:04:32.110
- One of the greatest
pieces of advice I've ever

00:04:32.110 --> 00:04:34.032
gotten in my life, was from my mom,

00:04:34.032 --> 00:04:36.445
when I was a little kid.

00:04:36.445 --> 00:04:39.083
There was a kid who was
bugging me in school,

00:04:39.083 --> 00:04:42.424
and she said okay, I'm going
to tell you what to do.

00:04:42.424 --> 00:04:44.453
She said the kid's bugging you.

00:04:44.453 --> 00:04:49.211
He puts his hands on you,
you pick up the nearest rock,

00:04:49.211 --> 00:04:52.082
or whatever you can get your
hands on, and you lay him out.

00:04:52.082 --> 00:04:55.309
(audience laughing)

00:04:55.309 --> 00:04:58.341
- [Audience Member] Yay mom!

00:04:58.341 --> 00:04:59.424
- Then I did.

00:05:00.840 --> 00:05:03.920
And I felt better, and it worked.

00:05:03.920 --> 00:05:07.170
And so for me, that was a great lesson.

00:05:10.521 --> 00:05:13.604
Because someone had invaded my space,

00:05:14.509 --> 00:05:16.759
invaded my being, you know?

00:05:18.143 --> 00:05:21.228
And he was doing something against me

00:05:21.228 --> 00:05:25.241
that I didn't want to be done, so I took

00:05:25.241 --> 00:05:28.908
control of the situation,
and I ran with it.

00:05:30.719 --> 00:05:34.052
And many years later, after being turned

00:05:35.454 --> 00:05:38.871
into a product by a very huge corporation

00:05:41.527 --> 00:05:43.596
that had their hands all over me,

00:05:43.596 --> 00:05:46.513
and I couldn't escape it, you know?

00:05:49.443 --> 00:05:53.768
I promised myself that I would
continue to move forward,

00:05:53.768 --> 00:05:57.935
and do my best not to compromise
in any way, whatsoever.

00:05:59.350 --> 00:06:02.747
Not allow anyone to put their hands on me.

00:06:02.747 --> 00:06:04.626
And effect me in that way.

00:06:04.626 --> 00:06:08.081
So that's the best advice
I think I could give,

00:06:08.081 --> 00:06:09.667
is just to keep moving forward, and don't

00:06:09.667 --> 00:06:11.826
give a (beep) what anybody thinks.

00:06:11.826 --> 00:06:13.661
Just keep moving forward and doing what

00:06:13.661 --> 00:06:15.626
you have to do, for you.

00:06:15.626 --> 00:06:18.637
- You know, I work in a
business where some people

00:06:18.637 --> 00:06:20.804
are a little bit arrogant.

00:06:22.127 --> 00:06:23.867
And maybe they're having a bad day,

00:06:23.867 --> 00:06:25.939
and I've seen this thing kind of happen,

00:06:25.939 --> 00:06:30.202
where you're on a film set,
and someone seems to be

00:06:30.202 --> 00:06:31.916
in a really bad mood, and they're treating

00:06:31.916 --> 00:06:33.428
people pretty badly.

00:06:33.428 --> 00:06:35.039
And generally you can
see that they're treating

00:06:35.039 --> 00:06:39.890
an extra badly, or a stand-in
badly, or a cameraman badly.

00:06:39.890 --> 00:06:41.526
No one ever confronts them.

00:06:41.526 --> 00:06:43.557
And I'm a big confronter.

00:06:43.557 --> 00:06:46.798
I will generally call a
meeting into my trailer.

00:06:46.798 --> 00:06:50.600
With producer, with either
the person who's causing

00:06:50.600 --> 00:06:54.600
what I think is unnecessary
tension and disruption.

00:06:54.600 --> 00:06:56.755
Or being particularly mean.

00:06:56.755 --> 00:07:00.868
And I will say, look,
I come here every day,

00:07:00.868 --> 00:07:03.099
to try to be a part of
creating an environment

00:07:03.099 --> 00:07:05.218
where we all can do our best work.

00:07:05.218 --> 00:07:07.868
And this behavior isn't going to fly.

00:07:07.868 --> 00:07:11.590
And what I often find, is
that it's when you confront

00:07:11.590 --> 00:07:15.552
someone who's behaving in
that kind of belaying fashion,

00:07:15.552 --> 00:07:17.191
that they're really stunned.

00:07:17.191 --> 00:07:19.494
Because normally, they
can get away with it.

00:07:19.494 --> 00:07:20.973
Because everyone's just
like, oh, they're in a

00:07:20.973 --> 00:07:23.175
really bad mood, what are we going to do?

00:07:23.175 --> 00:07:25.010
Oh my God, you talk to someone.

00:07:25.010 --> 00:07:28.061
And everyone's sort of
whispering, and sneaking around,

00:07:28.061 --> 00:07:29.848
instead of walking up to
that person and saying,

00:07:29.848 --> 00:07:32.310
what is your problem?

00:07:32.310 --> 00:07:34.060
What is your problem?

00:07:35.078 --> 00:07:37.369
Because your problem is
becoming our problem,

00:07:37.369 --> 00:07:39.541
and in fact, we were
having a really good time,

00:07:39.541 --> 00:07:43.475
until you entered the scene,
and created an environment

00:07:43.475 --> 00:07:48.089
that was unpleasant,
disruptive, and unnecessary.

00:07:48.089 --> 00:07:49.015
And you know what?

00:07:49.015 --> 00:07:50.852
It's not going to make
anyone work any faster,

00:07:50.852 --> 00:07:52.146
or any better.

00:07:52.146 --> 00:07:54.326
The ways in which you get people
to work faster and better,

00:07:54.326 --> 00:07:56.940
is to treat them as equals.

00:07:56.940 --> 00:08:00.342
And to treat them as people
who care about their work,

00:08:00.342 --> 00:08:01.752
and you care about your work.

00:08:01.752 --> 00:08:04.172
And it's only when people come together,

00:08:04.172 --> 00:08:06.391
that you can accomplish something.

00:08:06.391 --> 00:08:08.109
- If you've got somebody
that's bullying you.

00:08:08.109 --> 00:08:10.679
Like both of you got jumped on.

00:08:10.679 --> 00:08:13.002
You took steps, you reported,
you said the right things,

00:08:13.002 --> 00:08:17.170
you did the right things, and
you still got attacked, right?

00:08:17.170 --> 00:08:18.952
Is that fair?

00:08:18.952 --> 00:08:19.969
- No.

00:08:19.969 --> 00:08:21.264
- No way it's fair.

00:08:21.264 --> 00:08:24.043
When you go to somebody in authority,

00:08:24.043 --> 00:08:26.056
and you tell them what's going on,

00:08:26.056 --> 00:08:27.790
that's not tattling.

00:08:27.790 --> 00:08:29.731
You did the right things, Lily.

00:08:29.731 --> 00:08:30.864
Did the right things.

00:08:30.864 --> 00:08:32.446
And you still got attacked.

00:08:32.446 --> 00:08:35.976
The question is, what do you do when that

00:08:35.976 --> 00:08:37.438
unfair thing happens to you?

00:08:37.438 --> 00:08:40.164
Do you let that define you?

00:08:40.164 --> 00:08:41.566
Or you can say, well wait a minute.

00:08:41.566 --> 00:08:43.743
I got to be my own best friend here.

00:08:43.743 --> 00:08:47.101
I have the power to choose
how I feel about this.

00:08:47.101 --> 00:08:49.507
I'm not going to be embarrassed.

00:08:49.507 --> 00:08:53.506
I'm not going to be traumatized
for the rest of my life.

00:08:53.506 --> 00:08:55.357
Behaviors have a beginning and an end.

00:08:55.357 --> 00:08:56.574
You two got attacked.

00:08:56.574 --> 00:08:58.907
Lasted a few minutes, right?

00:08:59.903 --> 00:09:01.480
How long has it been?

00:09:01.480 --> 00:09:02.680
- Over a year.

00:09:02.680 --> 00:09:03.834
- Few months.

00:09:03.834 --> 00:09:07.414
- And you're still effected
by it today, right?

00:09:07.414 --> 00:09:08.590
- Yeah.

00:09:08.590 --> 00:09:12.770
- You have not given yourself
permission to get past it.

00:09:12.770 --> 00:09:14.420
You've not given yourself
permission to say,

00:09:14.420 --> 00:09:17.183
I encountered some sick
people, some small people,

00:09:17.183 --> 00:09:20.038
some petty people, some jealous people.

00:09:20.038 --> 00:09:22.198
I want you to change choices.

00:09:22.198 --> 00:09:24.582
You're already choosing
how you feel about it.

00:09:24.582 --> 00:09:27.117
If this is brought up to you,

00:09:27.117 --> 00:09:29.431
what are you going to say about it?

00:09:29.431 --> 00:09:31.445
Aren't you that girl that
got beat up on the tape?

00:09:31.445 --> 00:09:33.390
Yeah, it was one of the
worst times of my life.

00:09:33.390 --> 00:09:34.984
Did you have a question about it?

00:09:34.984 --> 00:09:36.592
Oh.

00:09:36.592 --> 00:09:37.492
You know what's going to happen?

00:09:37.492 --> 00:09:40.372
They're going to go,
oh, no, I guess I don't.

00:09:40.372 --> 00:09:42.839
This isn't something where
time heals all wounds.

00:09:42.839 --> 00:09:43.816
Time heals nothing.

00:09:43.816 --> 00:09:45.428
It's what you do with that time.

00:09:45.428 --> 00:09:46.261
Okay?

00:09:46.261 --> 00:09:48.176
What I want you to do,
is five years from now,

00:09:48.176 --> 00:09:51.260
I want you to look back
and say, that event became

00:09:51.260 --> 00:09:54.158
the springboard for me
being tough, focused,

00:09:54.158 --> 00:09:57.004
and able to other people move along.

00:09:57.004 --> 00:10:00.578
- Bullies prey on the weak to
feed their own insecurities.

00:10:00.578 --> 00:10:03.151
They can't do anything amazing themselves.

00:10:03.151 --> 00:10:05.893
They don't want to get into the
arena and follow their dreams,

00:10:05.893 --> 00:10:07.954
and so what they need
to do, is pull everybody

00:10:07.954 --> 00:10:09.260
down to their level.

00:10:09.260 --> 00:10:10.965
If somebody's here,
and somebody's up here,

00:10:10.965 --> 00:10:12.929
and you want to get
closer, it's either bring

00:10:12.929 --> 00:10:14.464
the people up with you, or try to

00:10:14.464 --> 00:10:15.764
tear the other people down.

00:10:15.764 --> 00:10:16.903
And that's what bullies do.

00:10:16.903 --> 00:10:19.389
And what they crave, is your response.

00:10:19.389 --> 00:10:21.261
They crave you reacting to it.

00:10:21.261 --> 00:10:22.094
That's what they want.

00:10:22.094 --> 00:10:23.356
They want to get under your skin.

00:10:23.356 --> 00:10:26.729
They want you to feel that
you're now at their level.

00:10:26.729 --> 00:10:28.975
They want to drag you back
down to where they are.

00:10:28.975 --> 00:10:30.408
They want to fight in the mud.

00:10:30.408 --> 00:10:32.341
And so the solution is,
don't give it to them.

00:10:32.341 --> 00:10:34.259
Again, they want to pull you down to feed

00:10:34.259 --> 00:10:35.691
their own insecurities.

00:10:35.691 --> 00:10:36.743
And if they don't get it from you,

00:10:36.743 --> 00:10:38.331
they're going to get
it from somebody else.

00:10:38.331 --> 00:10:40.426
And if you don't give it to
them, if you don't react,

00:10:40.426 --> 00:10:43.547
if you don't yell and
scream, or cry, or get upset,

00:10:43.547 --> 00:10:44.698
they're going to go somewhere
else, they're going to

00:10:44.698 --> 00:10:45.531
leave you alone.

00:10:45.531 --> 00:10:46.633
So stop reacting.

00:10:46.633 --> 00:10:49.206
This, at the start, may
be harder to actually do

00:10:49.206 --> 00:10:52.268
than to say, but it's a
simple, easy solution.

00:10:52.268 --> 00:10:53.904
Doesn't mean it's actually easy to do.

00:10:53.904 --> 00:10:56.868
But reminding yourself, before even you go

00:10:56.868 --> 00:10:59.332
into a situation, will
make it easier for you.

00:10:59.332 --> 00:11:00.688
So if you know that there's this person,

00:11:00.688 --> 00:11:02.557
who's always bullying you, and you have a

00:11:02.557 --> 00:11:04.975
meeting with them coming
up, remind yourself of it.

00:11:04.975 --> 00:11:06.512
Remind yourself, that
I'm not going to react.

00:11:06.512 --> 00:11:08.694
That this person's opinion doesn't matter.

00:11:08.694 --> 00:11:09.879
I'm not going to let them trigger me.

00:11:09.879 --> 00:11:11.911
Remind yourself of that
before the meeting,

00:11:11.911 --> 00:11:14.222
and going in will be easier for you to get

00:11:14.222 --> 00:11:15.885
the desired outcome that you want.

00:11:15.885 --> 00:11:17.986
And if you do that consistently,
they're going to realize,

00:11:17.986 --> 00:11:19.655
wow, this person doesn't care anymore,

00:11:19.655 --> 00:11:21.348
this person isn't triggered by me anymore.

00:11:21.348 --> 00:11:24.179
Huh, I'm not getting what I
need anymore from that person.

00:11:24.179 --> 00:11:25.779
I'm not feeding my own
insecurities anymore

00:11:25.779 --> 00:11:27.604
from that person, I'm
going to go somewhere else.

00:11:27.604 --> 00:11:28.894
I'm going to go pick on somebody else.

00:11:28.894 --> 00:11:29.841
That's what bullies do.

00:11:29.841 --> 00:11:32.490
I would strongly encourage you to stop

00:11:32.490 --> 00:11:34.509
living your life in the rear view mirror.

00:11:34.509 --> 00:11:37.596
People rip off my content,
as an example, all the time.

00:11:37.596 --> 00:11:40.542
People will post things
that I'm putting up

00:11:40.542 --> 00:11:41.964
on YouTube, on their channel.

00:11:41.964 --> 00:11:43.393
With credit, with no credit.

00:11:43.393 --> 00:11:44.770
They're trying to do
exactly what I'm doing.

00:11:44.770 --> 00:11:45.647
I don't care.

00:11:45.647 --> 00:11:46.985
People write to me all the time, like hey,

00:11:46.985 --> 00:11:49.085
this person took your
video, and posted them

00:11:49.085 --> 00:11:50.025
on their channel.

00:11:50.025 --> 00:11:51.907
You're not going to do better at being me,

00:11:51.907 --> 00:11:53.875
than I will be at being me.

00:11:53.875 --> 00:11:55.103
That's just not going to happen.

00:11:55.103 --> 00:11:58.178
And I can either choose
to spend all of my time,

00:11:58.178 --> 00:12:01.797
focusing on these people, and
just defending what I have,

00:12:01.797 --> 00:12:04.460
as opposed to going out and getting more.

00:12:04.460 --> 00:12:05.949
I'm not concerned with
somebody trying to be

00:12:05.949 --> 00:12:08.536
the next Evan Carmichael,
because you can't.

00:12:08.536 --> 00:12:11.247
But you can be a better
you, than I could be.

00:12:11.247 --> 00:12:12.661
That's where you need
to focus your energy.

00:12:12.661 --> 00:12:14.527
And so, I don't spend my time focusing

00:12:14.527 --> 00:12:15.551
in the rear view mirror.

00:12:15.551 --> 00:12:17.482
I don't care about
taking down those videos,

00:12:17.482 --> 00:12:19.024
or taking down those channels.

00:12:19.024 --> 00:12:21.107
What I care about is
the mission that I'm on,

00:12:21.107 --> 00:12:23.155
in helping you guys, and making more new,

00:12:23.155 --> 00:12:24.920
amazing, awesome videos.

00:12:24.920 --> 00:12:26.767
And so if you're spending
your time worrying about

00:12:26.767 --> 00:12:29.616
bullies, and dealing with
bullies, and reacting to bullies,

00:12:29.616 --> 00:12:31.125
then you're not spending your time

00:12:31.125 --> 00:12:34.391
focusing on big things
that you can do to grow.

00:12:34.391 --> 00:12:36.143
You're spending your life
in the rear view mirror,

00:12:36.143 --> 00:12:37.805
instead of driving forward.

00:12:37.805 --> 00:12:41.972
So stop spending you time,
in the rear view mirror.

00:12:44.097 --> 00:12:45.112
Thank you guys so much for watching.

00:12:45.112 --> 00:12:47.787
I made this video because
NeNeNa asked me to,

00:12:47.787 --> 00:12:49.381
so if there's a topic
you'd like me to cover

00:12:49.381 --> 00:12:51.204
in the next edition of Believe Life,

00:12:51.204 --> 00:12:52.356
leave it there in the comments below,

00:12:52.356 --> 00:12:53.409
and I'll see what I can do.

00:12:53.409 --> 00:12:54.912
I'd also love to know what did you think

00:12:54.912 --> 00:12:55.745
about this video?

00:12:55.745 --> 00:12:57.042
What did you lean from
this video that you can

00:12:57.042 --> 00:12:59.538
apply immediately to your
life, or to your business?

00:12:59.538 --> 00:13:02.130
How do you handle bullies,
that maybe we missed

00:13:02.130 --> 00:13:03.498
a point, that you can share.

00:13:03.498 --> 00:13:05.390
You can contribute back to Believe Nation,

00:13:05.390 --> 00:13:06.473
and share some knowledge as well,

00:13:06.473 --> 00:13:08.123
leave it there in the comments below,

00:13:08.123 --> 00:13:09.464
I'm going to join in the discussion.

00:13:09.464 --> 00:13:11.828
Finally, I want to give a
quick shout out to Matt McGill.

00:13:11.828 --> 00:13:13.472
Matt, thank you so much
for picking up a copy

00:13:13.472 --> 00:13:15.868
of my book, Your One
Word, and for reading it,

00:13:15.868 --> 00:13:17.556
and tweeting it out, I really appreciate

00:13:17.556 --> 00:13:19.452
the love and the support, man.

00:13:19.452 --> 00:13:20.657
So thank you guys so much for watching.

00:13:20.657 --> 00:13:21.668
I believe in you.

00:13:21.668 --> 00:13:23.827
I hope you continue to
believe in yourself,

00:13:23.827 --> 00:13:25.720
and whatever your one word is.

00:13:25.720 --> 00:13:29.348
Much love, have an amazing
day, and I'll see you soon.

00:13:29.348 --> 00:13:32.431
(dramatic crescendo)

00:13:35.551 --> 00:13:37.883
- There's no question, that individuals

00:13:37.883 --> 00:13:40.735
who are bystanders have more
power than they realize.

00:13:40.735 --> 00:13:43.871
Because most bullying
is going on for the joy

00:13:43.871 --> 00:13:45.184
of that person getting attention.

00:13:45.184 --> 00:13:46.215
It's a sense of power.

00:13:46.215 --> 00:13:47.558
If nobody notices them getting power,

00:13:47.558 --> 00:13:49.411
they don't feel a lot, you know?

00:13:49.411 --> 00:13:51.116
And for some people, who
are bullying the individual

00:13:51.116 --> 00:13:53.008
just by themself, but it's really rare.

00:13:53.008 --> 00:13:54.921
It's usually a pack mentality.

00:13:54.921 --> 00:13:57.020
And you don't have to be
bigger than that person,

00:13:57.020 --> 00:13:58.571
you don't have to pick a
fight with that person,

00:13:58.571 --> 00:14:00.591
all you have to do it, you
and two or three other people

00:14:00.591 --> 00:14:03.113
just go, this is not cool, or listen,

00:14:03.113 --> 00:14:04.614
we're going to call somebody, this is,

00:14:04.614 --> 00:14:05.855
dig this up some other time.

00:14:05.855 --> 00:14:08.213
Anything that you do, that
just breaks the pattern

00:14:08.213 --> 00:14:09.779
even for a moment, that's all it takes.

00:14:09.779 --> 00:14:10.931
'Cause people get in state.

00:14:10.931 --> 00:14:13.552
A bully, isn't always a bully
every moment of their life.

00:14:13.552 --> 00:14:14.970
You're going to meet
somebody that's a bully,

00:14:14.970 --> 00:14:16.864
in another environment, they
could be a really cool kid.

00:14:16.864 --> 00:14:18.674
But when they get in that
state of being a bully,

00:14:18.674 --> 00:14:20.428
it feeds on itself.

00:14:20.428 --> 00:14:22.433
So all it takes is a
little pattern unwrap.

00:14:22.433 --> 00:14:23.445
And a lot of people are afraid.

00:14:23.445 --> 00:14:24.793
Oh no, they're going to come attack me.

00:14:24.793 --> 00:14:26.607
They may threaten you, but you're not

00:14:26.607 --> 00:14:27.895
really their focus.

00:14:27.895 --> 00:14:29.923
That's not really what it is.

00:14:29.923 --> 00:14:31.189
And by the way, it happens with adults.

00:14:31.189 --> 00:14:32.328
It happens in a different way.

00:14:32.328 --> 00:14:35.478
It happens by rumors, and
things of that nature.

00:14:35.478 --> 00:14:36.701
It certainly happens to celebrities.

00:14:36.701 --> 00:14:39.086
I have a lot of celebrity
friends and clients,

00:14:39.086 --> 00:14:41.503
and I'll be at a party, and
somebody will say something,

00:14:41.503 --> 00:14:43.518
in the entertainment business especially,

00:14:43.518 --> 00:14:44.971
about this person, and I'll just say,

00:14:44.971 --> 00:14:46.696
you know what, I watch
other people around,

00:14:46.696 --> 00:14:47.781
I see two other people are friends,

00:14:47.781 --> 00:14:49.032
not say a word, and I'll
step up and say you know,

00:14:49.032 --> 00:14:50.722
that is total bs.

00:14:50.722 --> 00:14:52.176
You know that's bs.

00:14:52.176 --> 00:14:53.820
I know this person, they're my friend.

00:14:53.820 --> 00:14:55.354
What you're saying is
just completely made up.

00:14:55.354 --> 00:14:56.752
There's no truth to it whatsoever.

00:14:56.752 --> 00:14:57.585
Why would you do that?

00:14:57.585 --> 00:14:59.455
When you put the burn
back in that direction,

00:14:59.455 --> 00:15:01.619
(snaps) it's really
rapid how things change,

00:15:01.619 --> 00:15:03.198
'cause other people look around.

00:15:03.198 --> 00:15:05.938
What I tell people is,
don't tolerate behavior.

00:15:05.938 --> 00:15:07.767
You get what you tolerate.

00:15:07.767 --> 00:15:09.550
Don't tolerate behavior
from other human beings,

00:15:09.550 --> 00:15:13.207
that you personally would
not want for yourself.

00:15:13.207 --> 00:15:15.181
And so even if you're not
the one being bullied,

00:15:15.181 --> 00:15:16.275
don't tolerate it.

00:15:16.275 --> 00:15:17.108
Step up.

00:15:17.108 --> 00:15:18.584
And we could not tolerate it by the

00:15:18.584 --> 00:15:20.000
power of the third side.

00:15:20.000 --> 00:15:21.781
There's a person
attacking, there's a person

00:15:21.781 --> 00:15:24.189
being attacked, and
there's the third side.

00:15:24.189 --> 00:15:25.971
The third side can
surround it, and change it

00:15:25.971 --> 00:15:27.063
in two seconds.

00:15:27.063 --> 00:15:28.778
And I say, lead the third side.

00:15:28.778 --> 00:15:32.359
- For a long time, people
were talking about bully.

00:15:32.359 --> 00:15:34.141
And that was a big hot topic.

00:15:34.141 --> 00:15:36.840
And I think sometimes you can forget that

00:15:36.840 --> 00:15:38.740
you can be your own bully in some ways.

00:15:38.740 --> 00:15:40.105
You are the person that is standing

00:15:40.105 --> 00:15:42.547
in the way of your success, whether its

00:15:42.547 --> 00:15:44.668
professionally, or personally.

00:15:44.668 --> 00:15:47.741
And honestly, that was the case for me.

00:15:47.741 --> 00:15:50.005
I was having a great professional streak.

00:15:50.005 --> 00:15:51.817
But personally, I was really immature.

00:15:51.817 --> 00:15:54.260
And so I had to balance them out.

00:15:54.260 --> 00:15:56.521
Finally I had enough, and I said hey,

00:15:56.521 --> 00:15:58.566
you need to speak up for yourself.

00:15:58.566 --> 00:16:00.459
If you're not happy with
something, you change it.

00:16:00.459 --> 00:16:02.867
Change it, make yourself
better every single day.

00:16:02.867 --> 00:16:05.215
So I went to a lot of therapy.

00:16:05.215 --> 00:16:06.461
(laughs)

00:16:06.461 --> 00:16:10.194
And I guess I put it in
the way of you're going to

00:16:10.194 --> 00:16:11.029
hear me roar.

00:16:11.029 --> 00:16:13.655
Finally, I'm going to be
able to speak up for myself.

